{"id": "pattern-class-layer-remap-001", "type": "pattern", "fact": "A whole-app typography/colour migration was done without touching call sites by keeping the EXISTING utility class names (text-h1, text-body, text-price, ...) and remapping what they resolve to in the Tailwind plugin, then adding the new names alongside. That reduced the migration from 154 call sites to zero and let the new and old scales coexist while screens were converted one at a time.", "recommendation": "When replacing a design system, change what a class resolves to before changing where it is used, and keep legacy aliases in the token layer (legacyTypographyAliases in tokens.raw.js) until every call site has moved. Retire the aliases as a separate, mechanical commit.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "specs/017-ui-refresh self-reflect", "date": "2026-11-06"}], "tags": ["design-system", "migration", "nativewind", "refactoring"], "affectedFiles": ["mobile/tailwind.config.js", "mobile/src/theme/tokens.raw.js"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-11-06T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-11-06T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
